---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Felix Geelhaar — engineering leader writing Field Notes on shipping software with AI agents. Builds open-source Go libraries + Armada (Atlassian Marketplace)."
  lede="The long version."
  nav="about"
  ogImage="about"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <p>
      I write <strong>Field Notes</strong> &mdash; long-form essays on shipping software with AI
      agents. Plan-of-record, evidence layers, agent runtimes, the anti-patterns engineering
      teams ship when a model is in the loop, and the engineering practices that hold the rest
      of the work together when the model is wrong. Less framework, more field notes.
    </p>
    <p>
      In parallel I build the tools. A dozen open-source Go libraries on
      <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar">github.com/felixgeelhaar</a>, plus
      <a href={`${BASE}armada`}>Armada</a> (campaign orchestration for Jira, on the Atlassian
      Marketplace) &mdash; see <a href={`${BASE}lab`}>/lab</a> for the current shortlist.
    </p>
    <p>
      Background: 15+ years across engineering, platform, and ops roles &mdash; a mix of
      startups, scale-ups, and enterprise. Picked up JavaScript and PHP early, drifted into
      TypeScript, settled on Go for most things I ship today. I live near Munich. Currently
      focused on what's on <a href={`${BASE}now`}>/now</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Find me elsewhere</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar">GitHub</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/felixgeelhaar/">LinkedIn</a></li>
      <li><a href={`${BASE}contact`}>Email</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
